From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 09 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: force fedora variant for template rendering

Hummingbird OS is a Fedora derivative but cloud-init does not recognize
it. When building on a Hummingbird host the auto-detected variant falls
through to the generic "linux" default, which causes systemd templates
to render with incorrect paths (e.g. /usr/lib/cloud-init/ds-identify
instead of /usr/libexec/cloud-init/ds-identify).

Force the template renderer to default to the "fedora" variant so that
all paths match the Fedora filesystem layout.

---
 tools/render-template | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/render-template b/tools/render-template
index 1234567..abcdefg 100755
--- a/tools/render-template
+++ b/tools/render-template
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ def main():
     platform = util.system_info()
     parser.add_argument(
         "--variant",
-        default=platform["variant"],
+        default="fedora",
         action="store",
         help="define the variant.",
         choices=VARIANTS,
